  greedy minimum cover     : 78 pairs cover all 4413 lists
    the ten biggest        : [((7, 6), 630), ((14, 6), 489), ((16, 4), 422), ((7, 3), 292), ((21, 15), 238), ((7, 5), 221), ((14, 8), 220), ((7, 4), 167), ((14, 12), 166), ((28, 4), 149)]

READING.
  Every instance is the SAME statement -- 'every d in L lies in the band at (e,k)' --
  which is one theorem, clear_at_opening_of_band, instantiated. The 4,413 are
  membership checks against 169 distinct (flank, opening) pairs, and a greedy
  cover needs only 78 of them.

  So the 1,341 / 3,072 split ('at the bound' versus 'at a later opening') is a FALSE
  DIVISION: it is one criterion evaluated at different k, not two phenomena. And the
  spread of k is bounded by the flank -- the verdict is periodic in k with period e,
  confirmed 13,239 / 13,239, and no instance uses k >= e.
